    "result_text": "The full suite is green: **278 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented city normalization for owner creation.\n\n**New function class** \u2014 `NormalizeCity.java` (`rest/function/owner/`):\n- Reads the built `Owner` (`@Val`) and the `OwnerRepository`.\n- If an owner already exists in that city (case-insensitive match), it copies that existing owner's **exact** city spelling onto the new owner \u2014 so a city is spelt consistently across all its owners.\n- Otherwise it **title-cases** the city (each whitespace-separated word gets an upper-case first letter, the rest lower-cased, e.g. `\"riverdale5\"` \u2192 `\"Riverdale5\"`).\n- Null cities are left untouched.\n\n**Pipeline wiring** \u2014 `officefloor/rest/api/owners.POST.yml`:\n- Inserted a `normalizeCity` step between `build` and `ensureUnique`, under the existing `transaction` governance, so the normalized city flows through to uniqueness checks, customer-code assignment, saving and the response.\n\nPlacement is safe with respect to the existing per-city customer-code logic (`AssignCustomerCode`), which already matches cities case-insensitively, so `Cp10Tests` continues to pass alongside the new `Cp12Tests`.",
